{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\nsys.stderr = sys.stdout\n\ndef factorial_product(n, mod):\n    c = [0] * (n + 1)\n    c[n] = 1\n    for k in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        c[k] = (c[k + 1] * (k + 1)) % mod\n        if c[k] == 0:\n            break\n    return c\n\ndef build_tables(n, mod):\n    tables = [[[1]]]\n    for idx in range(n - 1):\n        old = tables[idx]\n        width = idx + 1\n        nrows = len(old) + width\n        new = [[0] * (width + 1) for _ in range(nrows)]\n        for j, row in enumerate(old):\n            for col, value in enumerate(row):\n                for off in range(width):\n                    new[j + off][col] = (new[j + off][col] + value) % mod\n                new[j + width][width] = (new[j + width][width] + value) % mod\n        tables.append(new)\n    return tables\n\ndef contribution(rows, mod, coeff):\n    R = len(rows)\n    D = len(rows[0])\n    pref = [[0] * D for _ in range(R)]\n    for j in range(R):\n        acc = 0\n        for col in range(D - 1, -1, -1):\n            acc = (acc + rows[j][col]) % mod\n            pref[j][col] = acc\n    for j in range(1, R):\n        for col in range(D):\n            pref[j][col] = (pref[j][col] + pref[j - 1][col]) % mod\n    total = 0\n    for j in range(1, R):\n        for col in range(D - 1):\n            total = (total + rows[j][col] * pref[j - 1][col + 1]) % mod\n    return (total * coeff) % mod\n\ndef solve(n, mod):\n    c = factorial_product(n, mod)\n    tables = build_tables(n, mod)\n    ans = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        ans = (ans + contribution(tables[i], mod, c[i + 1])) % mod\n    return ans\n\ndef main():\n    n, m = map(int, input().split())\n    print(solve(n, m))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cstdint>\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\n\nvector<ll> factorial_product(int n, ll mod) {\n    vector<ll> c(n + 1, 0);\n    c[n] = 1;\n    for (int k = n - 1; k >= 0; --k) {\n        c[k] = (c[k + 1] * (k + 1)) % mod;\n        if (c[k] == 0) break;\n    }\n    return c;\n}\n\nvector<vector<vector<ll>>> build_tables(int n, ll mod) {\n    vector<vector<vector<ll>>> tables;\n    tables.push_back({{1}});\n    for (int idx = 0; idx < n - 1; ++idx) {\n        const auto& old = tables[idx];\n        int width = idx + 1;\n        int nrows = (int)old.size() + width;\n        vector<vector<ll>> new_table(nrows, vector<ll>(width + 1, 0));\n        for (int j = 0; j < (int)old.size(); ++j) {\n            const auto& row = old[j];\n            for (int col = 0; col < (int)row.size(); ++col) {\n                ll value = row[col];\n                for (int off = 0; off < width; ++off) {\n                    new_table[j + off][col] = (new_table[j + off][col] + value) % mod;\n                }\n                new_table[j + width][width] = (new_table[j + width][width] + value) % mod;\n            }\n        }\n        tables.push_back(new_table);\n    }\n    return tables;\n}\n\nll contribution(const vector<vector<ll>>& rows, ll mod, ll coeff) {\n    int R = (int)rows.size();\n    int D = (int)rows[0].size();\n    vector<vector<ll>> pref(R, vector<ll>(D, 0));\n    for (int j = 0; j < R; ++j) {\n        ll acc = 0;\n        for (int col = D - 1; col >= 0; --col) {\n            acc = (acc + rows[j][col]) % mod;\n            pref[j][col] = acc;\n        }\n    }\n    for (int j = 1; j < R; ++j) {\n        for (int col = 0; col < D; ++col) {\n            pref[j][col] = (pref[j][col] + pref[j - 1][col]) % mod;\n        }\n    }\n    ll total = 0;\n    for (int j = 1; j < R; ++j) {\n        for (int col = 0; col < D - 1; ++col) {\n            total = (total + rows[j][col] * pref[j - 1][col + 1]) % mod;\n        }\n    }\n    return (total * coeff) % mod;\n}\n\nll solve(int n, ll mod) {\n    vector<ll> c = factorial_product(n, mod);\n    vector<vector<vector<ll>>> tables = build_tables(n, mod);\n    ll ans = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; ++i) {\n        ans = (ans + contribution(tables[i], mod, c[i + 1])) % mod;\n    }\n    return ans;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    ll m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    cout << solve(n, m) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.98\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.008879579603672028, -1.7881377516459906e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00016008525562938303, -0.00012766500003635883, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.0012469858629629016, -8.940656698541716e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.0265373677830212e-05, -3.5523738915799186e-05, 0.0, -0.12695544958114624, -0.00010084597306558862, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.3132949471473694, -0.47412604093551636, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -0.2014218121767044, -0.07548875361680984, -0.048632748425006866, 0.0, -5.793403761344962e-05, -0.00012814177898690104, -0.0002760506176855415, -1.0371154530730564e-05, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -0.02324579656124115, -2.264974000354414e-06, 0.0, -0.0001586549769854